WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:03.963
[MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31.407 --> 00:00:34.910
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

3
00:00:37.413 --> 00:00:38.414
[HEAVY BREATHING]

4
00:00:38.414 --> 00:00:39.415
[PHONE BUZZING]

5
00:00:39.415 --> 00:00:42.877
[PHONE RINGING]

6
00:00:45.379 --> 00:00:47.423
Huh.

7
00:00:47.423 --> 00:00:51.093
Toby, what's going on?

8
00:00:51.093 --> 00:00:54.221
So the sun slapped you in the face?

9
00:00:54.221 --> 00:00:55.973
Why didn't you call the Sheriff?

10
00:00:55.973 --> 00:00:56.849
Well, call him again.

11
00:01:00.728 --> 00:01:01.479
It's 6:00 AM.

12
00:01:01.479 --> 00:01:03.939
They should be in a U-Haul halfway out of Lawndale

13
00:01:03.939 --> 00:01:05.316
and not slapping you in the face.

14
00:01:05.316 --> 00:01:07.818
That's assault. 10-year-olds are just

15
00:01:07.818 --> 00:01:09.028
as dangerous as 20-year-olds.

16
00:01:09.028 --> 00:01:09.612
You know that.

17
00:01:13.115 --> 00:01:17.620
Hey, I've got to go.

18
00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:18.454
I'll call you later.

19
00:01:18.454 --> 00:01:21.874
[HUMPH]

20
00:01:25.336 --> 00:01:27.797
[GIGGLING]

21
00:01:27.797 --> 00:01:28.297
[KISS]

22
00:01:28.297 --> 00:01:32.218
[MOAN]

23
00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:40.100
[DRILL]

24
00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:45.022
[UGH] Just give me a moment.

25
00:01:45.022 --> 00:01:50.444
[SIGH] There is never a dull moment.

26
00:01:50.444 --> 00:01:52.404
Hm.

27
00:01:52.404 --> 00:01:54.490
I wasn't expecting you up so early.

28
00:01:54.490 --> 00:01:55.491
It's 4 o'clock.

29
00:01:55.491 --> 00:01:56.659
Half the day's behind us.

30
00:02:00.788 --> 00:02:02.456
You know who you look like?

31
00:02:02.456 --> 00:02:06.085
You look just like your father.

32
00:02:06.085 --> 00:02:10.673
You have the same nose

33
00:02:10.673 --> 00:02:12.550
Huh.

34
00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:14.552
Fortunately, that's all I inherited.

35
00:02:14.552 --> 00:02:17.137
What do you mean?

36
00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:19.974
He was never a provider, never really supported us.

37
00:02:19.974 --> 00:02:24.562
He just kind of left us to fend for ourselves.

38
00:02:24.562 --> 00:02:31.610
No milk money, no babysitting money, no gas money.

39
00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:36.282
He just hit the road after 10 years.

40
00:02:36.282 --> 00:02:39.785
You never even saw his feet hit the ground.

41
00:02:39.785 --> 00:02:44.290
Well, your feet are mounted in cement.

42
00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:49.378
Ariel is too fortunate to have you as an Uncle Richard.

43
00:02:49.378 --> 00:02:51.505
Sure.

44
00:02:51.505 --> 00:02:55.217
You know, I heard he ended some clown at Circus Circus

45
00:02:55.217 --> 00:02:57.303
when my mother sought payback for his philandering

46
00:02:57.303 --> 00:02:59.430
disposition.

47
00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:02.766
She got a girlfriend because he had so many.

48
00:03:02.766 --> 00:03:08.647
She got a boyfriend because he had so many girlfriends.

49
00:03:08.647 --> 00:03:10.357
He saw them going into this room,

50
00:03:10.357 --> 00:03:16.238
and he just transformed into quite a fellow.

51
00:03:16.238 --> 00:03:18.908
He pummeled the poor douche with a lead pipe

52
00:03:18.908 --> 00:03:21.118
and sent him into a coma for six months.

53
00:03:21.118 --> 00:03:24.038
He evaded the cops in a Bronco.

54
00:03:24.038 --> 00:03:26.123
Actually, I think it was a Corvette.

55
00:03:26.123 --> 00:03:27.416
It should have been a Bronco.

56
00:03:30.044 --> 00:03:38.093
He never harmed my mother like most jealous men would have.

57
00:03:38.093 --> 00:03:39.386
That's the last I heard of him.

58
00:03:42.306 --> 00:03:44.683
I wish I had known him.

59
00:03:44.683 --> 00:03:47.102
You know, I found a picture of him

60
00:03:47.102 --> 00:03:49.813
with my mom and another woman.

61
00:03:49.813 --> 00:03:51.857
He cheated with her too.

62
00:03:51.857 --> 00:03:59.865
She came to my mother's funeral, and cousin Ellen

63
00:03:59.865 --> 00:04:01.116
used to call her Aunt Yolanda.

64
00:04:05.371 --> 00:04:10.501
My mother would roll over in her grave if she saw me now.

65
00:04:10.501 --> 00:04:14.296
If she saw you now, she'd be proud of you.

66
00:04:14.296 --> 00:04:20.719
Because of my rolling estate, my Bowflex bod, or my trophy

67
00:04:20.719 --> 00:04:21.720
girlfriend?

68
00:04:24.515 --> 00:04:25.015
Shower?

69
00:04:25.015 --> 00:04:26.558
Mm.

70
00:04:26.558 --> 00:04:28.560
I like my space.

71
00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:29.561
[GIGGLING]

72
00:04:29.561 --> 00:04:32.982
All right.

73
00:04:32.982 --> 00:04:33.482
Whew.

74
00:04:45.369 --> 00:04:48.831
[WATER RUNNING]

75
00:04:55.713 --> 00:04:59.174
[MUSIC PLAYING]

76
00:05:10.728 --> 00:05:11.520
(OFFSCREEN) Dammit.

77
00:05:14.523 --> 00:05:18.027
[MUSIC PLAYING]

78
00:05:34.001 --> 00:05:35.002
(YELLING) Shit!

79
00:05:38.964 --> 00:05:40.466
[BANG]

80
00:05:40.466 --> 00:05:42.634
(OFFSCREEN) What's up?

81
00:05:42.634 --> 00:05:45.137
Bumped my knee.

82
00:05:45.137 --> 00:05:46.597
(OFFSCREEN) Be careful out there.

83
00:06:16.335 --> 00:06:20.130
Remember how you told me you despise CDs?

84
00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:26.220
Yeah.
It's weak interest, and short term,

85
00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:30.307
and it's not a sufficient investment.

86
00:06:30.307 --> 00:06:32.351
What would be sufficient?

87
00:06:32.351 --> 00:06:33.852
Where would you invest your money?

88
00:06:37.314 --> 00:06:38.315
Freshen up.

89
00:06:41.443 --> 00:06:43.195
Don't forget your glasses on your way out.

90
00:06:52.871 --> 00:06:55.999
You know, you said ask if I needed help.

91
00:06:55.999 --> 00:06:57.751
Well, your help is needed.

92
00:07:01.088 --> 00:07:01.588
Richard!

93
00:07:06.510 --> 00:07:08.595
So that's it, huh?

94
00:07:08.595 --> 00:07:10.305
That's our link?

95
00:07:10.305 --> 00:07:12.724
Staring at my Nordic tattoo while your pelvis

96
00:07:12.724 --> 00:07:15.978
smacks against my ass?

97
00:07:15.978 --> 00:07:18.063
You forgot to thank the Academy.

98
00:07:18.063 --> 00:07:21.358
You know, if you have issues, I've got short term loans.

99
00:07:21.358 --> 00:07:23.360
You can pay back, no interest.

100
00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:24.111
You're an asshole.

101
00:07:28.282 --> 00:07:31.660
[BANG]
[MUSIC PLAYING]

102
00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:33.912
Another fit of rage?

103
00:07:33.912 --> 00:07:35.247
You know my feelings about that.

104
00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:40.961
Money's frivolous.
Those were your words.

105
00:07:40.961 --> 00:07:42.379
You know, maybe we shouldn't date.

106
00:07:46.842 --> 00:07:48.343
Ruby?

107
00:07:48.343 --> 00:07:50.179
Ruby?

108
00:07:50.179 --> 00:07:51.180
Oh, no.

109
00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:19.791
[GRUNT]

110
00:08:21.752 --> 00:08:23.253
Don't forget the bags in the trunk.

111
00:08:23.253 --> 00:08:24.838
I can't wait to take a shower.

112
00:08:24.838 --> 00:08:25.380
Long night.

113
00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:27.341
Do you notice that mess on the garage floor?

114
00:08:27.341 --> 00:08:30.135
No.
Devin, check it out.

115
00:08:30.135 --> 00:08:31.428
It's eggshells.

116
00:08:31.428 --> 00:08:34.014
Probably that kid from across the street.

117
00:08:34.014 --> 00:08:36.600
Let's go inside.

118
00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:37.601
Oh, shit.

119
00:08:48.779 --> 00:08:52.199
[DOOR SQUEAKING]

120
00:08:52.199 --> 00:08:54.493
Oh, I'm glad Grandma's fine.

121
00:08:54.493 --> 00:08:55.953
[INAUDIBLE]?

122
00:08:55.953 --> 00:08:56.787
Not much.

123
00:08:56.787 --> 00:08:58.288
Smoking is prohibited.

124
00:08:58.288 --> 00:09:00.749
At Bennigan's the cops tasered some World War II geezer

125
00:09:00.749 --> 00:09:02.834
for puffing on a Colombian.

126
00:09:02.834 --> 00:09:03.335
Gosh.

127
00:09:03.335 --> 00:09:05.045
Where's you boyfriend?

128
00:09:05.045 --> 00:09:07.839
Devin, what's the problem?

129
00:09:07.839 --> 00:09:08.674
The bag got stuck.

130
00:09:08.674 --> 00:09:10.175
Where do you want them, Mrs. Warren?

131
00:09:10.175 --> 00:09:11.385
Not there.
Upstairs.

132
00:09:11.385 --> 00:09:12.302
Oh, it's OK, Devin.

133
00:09:12.302 --> 00:09:13.971
Just put it in the closet.

134
00:09:13.971 --> 00:09:14.972
Richard!

135
00:09:14.972 --> 00:09:16.139
Did you ask him?

136
00:09:16.139 --> 00:09:18.517
Not yet, but I will.

137
00:09:18.517 --> 00:09:20.394
Oh, are you guys hungry?

138
00:09:20.394 --> 00:09:21.979
No.
We are.

139
00:09:21.979 --> 00:09:22.896
Ariel.

140
00:09:22.896 --> 00:09:24.147
A little.

141
00:09:24.147 --> 00:09:26.525
[UGH] Go make him something.

142
00:09:26.525 --> 00:09:27.734
I'm going upstairs to change.

143
00:09:36.618 --> 00:09:38.120
[KNOCKING]

144
00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:40.831
Richard?

145
00:09:40.831 --> 00:09:42.207
[KNOCKING]

146
00:09:42.207 --> 00:09:44.042
Richard.
[CLEARS THROAT]

147
00:09:44.042 --> 00:09:45.711
[KNOCKING]
Richard.

148
00:09:45.711 --> 00:09:46.962
[GRUNT]

149
00:09:46.962 --> 00:09:48.547
I was sleeping.

150
00:09:48.547 --> 00:09:49.631
Do you mind?

151
00:09:49.631 --> 00:09:50.632
You're home early.

152
00:09:50.632 --> 00:09:51.258
I know.

153
00:09:51.258 --> 00:09:52.217
I'm tired.

154
00:10:01.435 --> 00:10:03.103
This is shameful.

155
00:10:03.103 --> 00:10:05.772
I'm sorry.
I was expecting you tomorrow.

156
00:10:12.612 --> 00:10:15.574
TSA let you on board with that?

157
00:10:15.574 --> 00:10:18.035
Ariel just gave it back.

158
00:10:18.035 --> 00:10:22.289
[SIGH] How was your trip?

159
00:10:22.289 --> 00:10:23.373
Exhausting.

160
00:10:27.669 --> 00:10:29.588
What time are Jahira and Fernando coming?

161
00:10:29.588 --> 00:10:31.590
Oh, 30 minutes.

162
00:10:31.590 --> 00:10:32.424
30 minutes?

163
00:10:32.424 --> 00:10:33.925
Uh-huh.

164
00:10:33.925 --> 00:10:34.676
You're home early.

165
00:10:34.676 --> 00:10:37.304
[GRUNT] I caught an earlier flight.

166
00:10:37.304 --> 00:10:41.308
Don't you check your voicemail?

167
00:10:41.308 --> 00:10:42.434
Ariel and Devin downstairs?

168
00:10:42.434 --> 00:10:44.519
Mm-hm.

169
00:10:44.519 --> 00:10:45.937
When are they leaving?

170
00:10:45.937 --> 00:10:46.980
I don't know.

171
00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:47.647
30 minutes?

172
00:10:57.866 --> 00:10:59.951
Did you have to hang your things here?

173
00:10:59.951 --> 00:11:01.953
They reek of garlic.

174
00:11:01.953 --> 00:11:04.664
You want to bathe in it?

175
00:11:04.664 --> 00:11:05.999
I'm going to go to the study.

176
00:11:08.752 --> 00:11:12.339
Oh, Ariel has something to ask you.

177
00:11:12.339 --> 00:11:15.842
[MUSIC PLAYING]

178
00:11:39.741 --> 00:11:43.245
[DISHES RATTLING]

179
00:11:48.708 --> 00:11:49.501
Hey!

180
00:11:49.501 --> 00:11:52.045
You look fit.

181
00:11:52.045 --> 00:11:53.255
Bowflex has been kind.

182
00:11:53.255 --> 00:11:56.133
I was going to come up there, but you came down here.

183
00:11:56.133 --> 00:11:56.633
Wow.

184
00:11:59.302 --> 00:12:00.971
No, Devin.
No, not that one.

185
00:12:00.971 --> 00:12:01.763
The other one.

186
00:12:01.763 --> 00:12:03.306
No, the other one.

187
00:12:03.306 --> 00:12:04.266
When are you leaving?

188
00:12:04.266 --> 00:12:05.058
Just give it to me.

189
00:12:05.058 --> 00:12:06.184
After this.
Where?

190
00:12:06.184 --> 00:12:08.270
Lake Elsinore.

191
00:12:08.270 --> 00:12:11.189
Yo, Doug, you see that order?

192
00:12:11.189 --> 00:12:14.151
Keep in that order.

193
00:12:14.151 --> 00:12:16.194
Excuse us a second.

194
00:12:16.194 --> 00:12:19.656
[PHONE NOTIFICATION]

195
00:12:22.117 --> 00:12:22.909
Go to the car.

196
00:12:26.329 --> 00:12:26.830
Sir.

197
00:12:30.417 --> 00:12:32.085
OK, I have a favor.

198
00:12:32.085 --> 00:12:33.628
I was wondering.

199
00:12:33.628 --> 00:12:35.464
Mm.

200
00:12:35.464 --> 00:12:36.590
You can't stand.

201
00:12:36.590 --> 00:12:37.757
You really want money?

202
00:12:37.757 --> 00:12:39.759
You can't stand on your feet?

203
00:12:39.759 --> 00:12:42.012
What's a student to do?

204
00:12:42.012 --> 00:12:43.096
Work for me.

205
00:12:43.096 --> 00:12:46.600
Only a celery stick is in my fridge, and a dollar in my bank

206
00:12:46.600 --> 00:12:47.100
account.

207
00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:48.560
Why are you going to Lake Elsinore?

208
00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:49.686
Is that paying for it?

209
00:12:49.686 --> 00:12:53.857
Yeah, paying he is, but LAUSD displaced him.

210
00:12:53.857 --> 00:12:57.527
[SIGH] How much?

211
00:12:57.527 --> 00:12:58.612
$500.

212
00:12:58.612 --> 00:12:59.863
I'll hit you back.

213
00:12:59.863 --> 00:13:01.615
I can't keep bailing you out.

214
00:13:01.615 --> 00:13:03.074
I need this break.

215
00:13:03.074 --> 00:13:06.286
I've given you thousands of dollars of breaks.

216
00:13:06.286 --> 00:13:06.786
Please.

217
00:13:10.248 --> 00:13:14.794
[UGH] OK, you're right.

218
00:13:14.794 --> 00:13:16.296
What are you doing?

219
00:13:16.296 --> 00:13:17.297
No money, no trip.

220
00:13:17.297 --> 00:13:19.633
You're right.
I need to start learning to cut back.

221
00:13:19.633 --> 00:13:22.886
So me and Devin will just stay here and watch TV.

222
00:13:25.555 --> 00:13:26.056
Here.

223
00:13:31.811 --> 00:13:32.687
Thank you.

224
00:13:32.687 --> 00:13:34.981
Put $1,500 in your account for Monday.

225
00:13:34.981 --> 00:13:36.191
Will that hold you?

226
00:13:36.191 --> 00:13:37.526
Yes.

227
00:13:37.526 --> 00:13:38.568
How's school?

228
00:13:38.568 --> 00:13:39.152
Awesome.

229
00:13:39.152 --> 00:13:40.237
I took your advice.

230
00:13:40.237 --> 00:13:41.988
I changed my major to business.

231
00:13:41.988 --> 00:13:43.657
America is capital, like you said.

232
00:13:43.657 --> 00:13:46.618
Right.

233
00:13:46.618 --> 00:13:49.996
[SIGH] You better get moving.

234
00:13:49.996 --> 00:13:53.375
Traffic is going to be fast and busy.

235
00:13:53.375 --> 00:13:55.585
Here you go.

236
00:13:55.585 --> 00:13:56.878
Thank you.

237
00:13:56.878 --> 00:13:57.379
Yes.

238
00:14:02.384 --> 00:14:05.845
[INAUDIBLE]

239
00:14:05.845 --> 00:14:06.346
Yay.

240
00:14:12.852 --> 00:14:18.817
[SIGH] See you around.

241
00:14:25.824 --> 00:14:29.327
[SIGH]

242
00:14:34.791 --> 00:14:38.295
[CAR ENGINE STARTING]

243
00:14:38.295 --> 00:14:41.798
[MUSIC PLAYING]

244
00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:10.744
[DOORBELL RINGING]

245
00:15:26.676 --> 00:15:30.180
[DOORBELL RINGING]

246
00:15:46.821 --> 00:15:48.615
Can I help you, Officer?

247
00:15:48.615 --> 00:15:50.575
Is that a yacht?

248
00:15:50.575 --> 00:15:52.410
It's a boat.

249
00:15:52.410 --> 00:15:53.995
Is there something I can do for you?

250
00:15:53.995 --> 00:15:55.538
Are you Mr. Warren?

251
00:15:55.538 --> 00:15:56.331
Yeah.

252
00:15:56.331 --> 00:15:57.248
Is there a problem?

253
00:15:57.248 --> 00:16:00.710
Yeah, well, my unit pursued a degenerate this morning.

254
00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:03.254
And she nabbed that car right outside your driveway.

255
00:16:03.254 --> 00:16:05.590
And we received a tip that she is sequestered somewhere

256
00:16:05.590 --> 00:16:07.092
in this neighborhood.

257
00:16:07.092 --> 00:16:08.093
Have you heard anything?

258
00:16:11.721 --> 00:16:14.099
This is a recent photograph of the suspect.

259
00:16:14.099 --> 00:16:15.475
Do you recognize her?

260
00:16:15.475 --> 00:16:16.601
Wow.

261
00:16:16.601 --> 00:16:19.896
What is big glasses?

262
00:16:19.896 --> 00:16:21.773
Yeah, she resembles Ugly Betty.

263
00:16:21.773 --> 00:16:24.484
But you know, those glasses are where that resemblance ends.

264
00:16:24.484 --> 00:16:26.945
Her antics resemble La Femme Nikita.

265
00:16:26.945 --> 00:16:28.947
She's treacherous, she's a complete [? goon, ?]

266
00:16:28.947 --> 00:16:30.365
and she's a sociopath.

267
00:16:30.365 --> 00:16:32.534
She leaves wallets, slits throats,

268
00:16:32.534 --> 00:16:35.203
and smiles just break in a new butterfly knife.

269
00:16:35.203 --> 00:16:38.581
Now, if you don't mind, I'd like to search your home.

270
00:16:38.581 --> 00:16:41.918
You're not a captive, are you?

271
00:16:41.918 --> 00:16:43.253
No.

272
00:16:43.253 --> 00:16:45.922
She has not been tickling my throat

273
00:16:45.922 --> 00:16:47.215
with her butterfly knife.

274
00:16:47.215 --> 00:16:48.925
Besides, don't you need a search warrant?

275
00:16:48.925 --> 00:16:50.260
Not with your permission.

276
00:16:53.096 --> 00:16:56.141
Is there a problem, mister?

277
00:16:56.141 --> 00:16:59.811
Maybe because we received word that we will barricade

278
00:16:59.811 --> 00:17:02.564
this neighborhood if anything suspicious or anyone acts

279
00:17:02.564 --> 00:17:03.314
suspicious.

280
00:17:03.314 --> 00:17:05.400
You know what?
I-

281
00:17:05.400 --> 00:17:07.402
Listen, I know it's an inconvenience,

282
00:17:07.402 --> 00:17:09.529
but sorry for the trouble.

283
00:17:09.529 --> 00:17:12.115
It may be a false alarm, but it's a pain in the ass.

284
00:17:12.115 --> 00:17:13.825
But your safety is my concern.

285
00:17:13.825 --> 00:17:16.202
Yet my C.O. insists.

286
00:17:16.202 --> 00:17:17.829
She may already have fled the area,

287
00:17:17.829 --> 00:17:20.039
and one can't be too sure.

288
00:17:20.039 --> 00:17:22.375
I just want to be sure we could check off your property,

289
00:17:22.375 --> 00:17:24.544
and make sure she's not camouflaged in the walk-in

290
00:17:24.544 --> 00:17:25.587
somewhere.

291
00:17:25.587 --> 00:17:27.589
Yes?

292
00:17:27.589 --> 00:17:28.089
Sure.

293
00:17:33.094 --> 00:17:36.514
Are you expecting any guests?

294
00:17:36.514 --> 00:17:38.600
Just my housekeepers.

295
00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:39.350
When are they due?

296
00:17:42.270 --> 00:17:43.855
10, 15 minutes.

297
00:17:43.855 --> 00:17:48.318
Why, Officer Murphy?

298
00:17:48.318 --> 00:17:49.027
Just be a moment.

299
00:17:52.238 --> 00:17:56.868
Listen, the potato head across the street

300
00:17:56.868 --> 00:18:02.832
always makes bogus phone calls, sends

301
00:18:02.832 --> 00:18:05.418
illustrious cops on wild goose chases.

302
00:18:05.418 --> 00:18:12.842
[LAUGHS] Well, thankfully, illustrious doesn't include me.

303
00:18:12.842 --> 00:18:14.219
Can I go upstairs?

304
00:18:14.219 --> 00:18:15.345
Can I tag along?

305
00:18:15.345 --> 00:18:16.179
It's your house.

306
00:18:20.642 --> 00:18:24.729
Tell me, mister, how much is this place worth?

307
00:18:24.729 --> 00:18:26.606
That's a reason?

308
00:18:26.606 --> 00:18:28.817
$10 to $12 million.

309
00:18:28.817 --> 00:18:32.278
AKA, just mind my business.

310
00:18:32.278 --> 00:18:56.261
Got it, Mr.

311
00:18:56.261 --> 00:18:59.722
[HAIRDRYER]

312
00:19:01.724 --> 00:19:03.726
Is someone taking a shower?

313
00:19:03.726 --> 00:19:05.061
That's my better half.

314
00:19:05.061 --> 00:19:06.604
May I?

315
00:19:06.604 --> 00:19:07.105
Sure.

316
00:19:10.984 --> 00:19:14.404
[HAIRDRYER]

317
00:19:15.864 --> 00:19:20.243
[KNOCKING]

318
00:19:20.243 --> 00:19:21.286
I'm sorry.

319
00:19:21.286 --> 00:19:24.706
I'm basically intercepting a call.

320
00:19:24.706 --> 00:19:25.206
OK.

321
00:19:25.206 --> 00:19:27.041
Um.

322
00:19:27.041 --> 00:19:29.294
Is everything fine?

323
00:19:29.294 --> 00:19:32.005
Everything is fine.

324
00:19:32.005 --> 00:19:33.756
I'm just concerned for your safety.

325
00:19:33.756 --> 00:19:34.340
Mm-hm.

326
00:19:34.340 --> 00:19:39.929
One other thing, do you recognize this person?

327
00:19:39.929 --> 00:19:41.472
No.

328
00:19:41.472 --> 00:19:44.642
But if I see her, you'll be the first to know.

329
00:19:44.642 --> 00:19:46.227
Officer, I think that's a whole house.

330
00:19:46.227 --> 00:19:47.729
(PHONE) You have a new text message.

331
00:19:47.729 --> 00:19:49.022
Sorry.

332
00:19:49.022 --> 00:19:50.982
Excuse me.
I have to take this call.

333
00:19:59.198 --> 00:20:01.618
[CLICK]

334
00:20:01.618 --> 00:20:03.411
Sorry about that.

335
00:20:03.411 --> 00:20:04.495
Where were we?

336
00:20:04.495 --> 00:20:07.081
I said, I think that's the whole house.

337
00:20:07.081 --> 00:20:09.751
I really don't think so.

338
00:20:13.671 --> 00:20:14.380
It smells.

339
00:20:14.380 --> 00:20:16.507
Why do you think my wife was in there?

340
00:20:16.507 --> 00:20:17.800
I can take it if you can.

341
00:20:17.800 --> 00:20:19.302
Officer, my time.

342
00:20:19.302 --> 00:20:20.345
Is there a problem, Mr.?

343
00:20:23.056 --> 00:20:25.224
I'll be quick.
Then I'll be out of your hair.

344
00:20:32.148 --> 00:20:35.652
[MUSIC PLAYING]

345
00:21:17.944 --> 00:21:19.570
You wear glasses?

346
00:21:19.570 --> 00:21:20.196
It's my wife's.

347
00:21:34.419 --> 00:21:36.838
What are you doing?

348
00:21:36.838 --> 00:21:37.630
I'm almost done.

349
00:21:42.093 --> 00:21:44.595
Officer, whoever you're looking for isn't here,

350
00:21:44.595 --> 00:21:45.847
so let's just call it a day.

351
00:21:45.847 --> 00:21:47.473
OK?

352
00:21:47.473 --> 00:21:47.974
Ma'am.

353
00:22:00.028 --> 00:22:05.616
Richard, next time, make sure your house

354
00:22:05.616 --> 00:22:06.826
guest remembers her glasses.

355
00:22:12.081 --> 00:22:15.501
[SLAM]

356
00:22:17.962 --> 00:22:19.964
Well, I guess the perpetrator isn't here.

357
00:22:19.964 --> 00:22:23.301
Well, maybe she's at another house.

358
00:22:23.301 --> 00:22:24.427
Maybe.

359
00:22:24.427 --> 00:22:28.431
But you know what I find funny, Mr., and find very surprising?

360
00:22:28.431 --> 00:22:29.307
Your wife's reaction.

361
00:22:29.307 --> 00:22:31.059
[LAUGHS] It's PMS.

362
00:22:33.811 --> 00:22:34.437
You know what?

363
00:22:34.437 --> 00:22:37.482
I confronted my ex-wife about the same similar situation,

364
00:22:37.482 --> 00:22:39.984
and she had said that the suit had magically

365
00:22:39.984 --> 00:22:42.320
appeared in my closet.

366
00:22:42.320 --> 00:22:44.781
She said it was magic.

367
00:22:44.781 --> 00:22:48.076
You two must have apprenticed with the same magician.

368
00:22:48.076 --> 00:22:50.578
OK, good day, Mr. Warren.

369
00:23:21.442 --> 00:23:23.361
(ANNOUNCER ON TV) This is field reporter Terry

370
00:23:23.361 --> 00:23:26.572
Handelman coming to you live from Carson, California.

371
00:23:26.572 --> 00:23:28.241
I'm standing in front of this residence

372
00:23:28.241 --> 00:23:31.035
where a large crowd has chained themselves to a fence,

373
00:23:31.035 --> 00:23:34.038
while the L.A. County Sheriffs post in front of the house.

374
00:23:34.038 --> 00:23:36.582
This is in response to an initial conflict beginning

375
00:23:36.582 --> 00:23:38.960
early this morning when the residents assaulted

376
00:23:38.960 --> 00:23:42.004
this man after refusing to vacate the property.

377
00:23:42.004 --> 00:23:43.923
First, can you tell us your name, sir?

378
00:23:43.923 --> 00:23:45.842
(MAN ON TV) Sure Toby Mitchell.

379
00:23:45.842 --> 00:23:46.425
(ANNOUNCER ON TV) Mr. Mitchell.

380
00:23:46.425 --> 00:23:47.510
(MAN ON TV) Please, call me Toby.

381
00:23:47.510 --> 00:23:48.219
(ANNOUNCER ON TV) OK, Toby.

382
00:23:48.219 --> 00:23:49.011
[GASP]
Shut up.

383
00:23:49.011 --> 00:23:50.680
It's not what you think.

384
00:23:50.680 --> 00:23:52.098
Is that the woman in that picture?

385
00:23:52.098 --> 00:23:53.850
Yes.
She knocked on the door and asked for help.

386
00:23:53.850 --> 00:23:56.018
[INAUDIBLE],, she was totally beaten dead.

387
00:23:56.018 --> 00:23:57.979
And nearsighted?

388
00:23:57.979 --> 00:23:59.438
You.

389
00:23:59.438 --> 00:24:01.399
You had to bring one of them here?

390
00:24:01.399 --> 00:24:02.525
So you kill her?

391
00:24:02.525 --> 00:24:03.025
No, no, no.

392
00:24:03.025 --> 00:24:04.443
I did not kill anyone.

393
00:24:04.443 --> 00:24:06.404
So I can ask them to go.

394
00:24:06.404 --> 00:24:07.864
Oh, my god.

395
00:24:07.864 --> 00:24:09.490
She's only been dead for a few minutes.

396
00:24:09.490 --> 00:24:10.366
I can take her to the hospital.

397
00:24:10.366 --> 00:24:12.076
They'll believe it was an accident.

398
00:24:12.076 --> 00:24:13.369
No one has to go to jail.

399
00:24:13.369 --> 00:24:14.871
You won't have to go to jail?

400
00:24:14.871 --> 00:24:16.372
Listen, cover for me.

401
00:24:16.372 --> 00:24:17.498
OK?
Please.

402
00:24:17.498 --> 00:24:18.082
I need you.

403
00:24:18.082 --> 00:24:19.584
(ANNOUNCER ON TV) There are millions

404
00:24:19.584 --> 00:24:21.419
of people who are victims of mortgage fraud.

405
00:24:21.419 --> 00:24:22.795
(MAN ON TV) Victims?

406
00:24:22.795 --> 00:24:24.213
Now they're the victims?

407
00:24:24.213 --> 00:24:28.050
I'm the one who got sucker punched by a fifth grader,

408
00:24:28.050 --> 00:24:29.802
in the balls, too.

409
00:24:29.802 --> 00:24:32.138
Can I see that on TV?

410
00:24:32.138 --> 00:24:34.557
Where are the cops?

411
00:24:34.557 --> 00:24:36.058
They should have been here.

412
00:24:41.397 --> 00:24:43.232
Fernando, Jahira.

413
00:24:43.232 --> 00:24:44.066
Buenos dias, senor.

414
00:24:44.066 --> 00:24:46.444
Good morning.
Good morning.

415
00:24:46.444 --> 00:24:47.570
Ready to work?

416
00:24:47.570 --> 00:24:48.070
Yes.

417
00:24:48.070 --> 00:24:49.447
We'll be in and out really quick.

418
00:24:49.447 --> 00:24:53.618
Listen, I've got something for you.

419
00:24:53.618 --> 00:24:55.578
Today, you get the day off.

420
00:24:55.578 --> 00:24:59.081
[SPEAKING SPANISH] We so need the day off.

421
00:24:59.081 --> 00:25:01.000
My sister is about to have my sobrino.

422
00:25:01.000 --> 00:25:03.211
We could use the day off.

423
00:25:03.211 --> 00:25:05.046
Would we be paid?

424
00:25:05.046 --> 00:25:06.464
Hm.

425
00:25:06.464 --> 00:25:09.217
No, not if you don't stay.

426
00:25:14.138 --> 00:25:17.642
[MUSIC PLAYING]

427
00:26:05.731 --> 00:26:08.651
How long is this going to take?

428
00:26:08.651 --> 00:26:10.236
10, 15 minutes.

429
00:26:14.156 --> 00:26:15.157
Do you need us to hurry?

430
00:26:15.157 --> 00:26:16.951
Mm.

431
00:26:16.951 --> 00:26:17.827
No.

432
00:26:17.827 --> 00:26:18.327
No hurry.

433
00:26:22.707 --> 00:26:24.792
Can we discuss my salary?

434
00:26:24.792 --> 00:26:25.960
Salary?

435
00:26:25.960 --> 00:26:26.502
Now?

436
00:26:26.502 --> 00:26:28.212
Yes, sir.

437
00:26:28.212 --> 00:26:30.089
[SIGH] Just give me a few minutes.

438
00:26:36.387 --> 00:26:38.347
Whew.

439
00:26:38.347 --> 00:26:39.807
Hey!

440
00:26:39.807 --> 00:26:42.143
Hey!

441
00:26:42.143 --> 00:26:43.811
Hey.

442
00:26:43.811 --> 00:26:45.688
[LAUGHS]

443
00:26:45.688 --> 00:26:46.647
Hey, senor.

444
00:26:46.647 --> 00:26:48.649
Conversation seems interesting.

445
00:26:48.649 --> 00:26:51.027
Si.

446
00:26:51.027 --> 00:26:53.029
[SIGH]

447
00:26:53.029 --> 00:26:54.613
Well, senora and I were just talking

448
00:26:54.613 --> 00:26:57.366
about how you can't wait for sobrina to have babies.

449
00:26:57.366 --> 00:26:59.827
Yeah.
Hm.

450
00:26:59.827 --> 00:27:00.828
Really?

451
00:27:00.828 --> 00:27:02.288
While vacuuming?

452
00:27:04.999 --> 00:27:07.126
Fine, you caught me.

453
00:27:07.126 --> 00:27:09.128
I didn't say anything.

454
00:27:09.128 --> 00:27:12.381
I was just here, listening to her.

455
00:27:12.381 --> 00:27:15.760
But then, you know, I told her that I really have to finish.

456
00:27:15.760 --> 00:27:16.427
Oh.

457
00:27:16.427 --> 00:27:18.679
Are you finished now?

458
00:27:18.679 --> 00:27:20.056
[? Yeah. ?]

459
00:27:20.056 --> 00:27:21.349
Go clean the other rooms.

460
00:27:21.349 --> 00:27:24.727
Yeah.
[INAUDIBLE]

461
00:27:24.727 --> 00:27:28.064
[SIGH]

462
00:27:32.151 --> 00:27:33.778
I thought you were getting rid of them.

463
00:27:33.778 --> 00:27:34.320
Ex that.

464
00:27:34.320 --> 00:27:38.074
I hope you didn't say anything.

465
00:27:38.074 --> 00:27:40.159
I don't want to ruin your life, but I'm leaving.

466
00:27:40.159 --> 00:27:41.619
Just give me your cell phone.

467
00:27:41.619 --> 00:27:42.411
What are you doing?

468
00:27:42.411 --> 00:27:45.331
Give it back.
Listen, a cop's outside.

469
00:27:45.331 --> 00:27:48.000
None of us can leave right now.

470
00:27:48.000 --> 00:27:53.381
I can't let you leave.
Look, if I send them home now, or if one of us splits,

471
00:27:53.381 --> 00:27:55.132
this guy's going to get suspicious.

472
00:27:55.132 --> 00:27:57.760
So please.

473
00:27:57.760 --> 00:27:59.136
You have 15 minutes.

474
00:28:02.890 --> 00:28:03.516
You're a jerk.

475
00:28:09.688 --> 00:28:11.565
Mr. Warren, can I speak with you, please?

476
00:28:23.869 --> 00:28:25.913
I'd like to renegotiate our rate.

477
00:28:25.913 --> 00:28:28.290
Renegotiate now?

478
00:28:28.290 --> 00:28:30.793
Until we do, I won't return.

479
00:28:30.793 --> 00:28:32.545
In case you haven't been scoping the news,

480
00:28:32.545 --> 00:28:35.464
the unemployment office has a line around the block.

481
00:28:35.464 --> 00:28:37.925
So I hope this wasn't a threat.

482
00:28:37.925 --> 00:28:39.677
I'm not threatening you, sir.

483
00:28:39.677 --> 00:28:42.555
We're just dissatisfied with the arrangements.

484
00:28:42.555 --> 00:28:44.849
Dissatisfied with a stud like you?

485
00:28:44.849 --> 00:28:46.517
Your wife should be satisfied.

486
00:28:46.517 --> 00:28:47.435
Not cool.

487
00:28:47.435 --> 00:28:50.563
Listen, right now is not the time, Fernando.

488
00:28:50.563 --> 00:28:51.939
Then we leave.

489
00:28:51.939 --> 00:28:52.773
Jahira!

490
00:28:52.773 --> 00:28:53.524
Jahira!

491
00:28:53.524 --> 00:28:54.984
[SIGH] How much?

492
00:28:59.989 --> 00:29:02.533
$250 per month.

493
00:29:02.533 --> 00:29:04.869
That sounds steep.

494
00:29:04.869 --> 00:29:06.412
So were those stairs I just vacuumed.

495
00:29:09.248 --> 00:29:11.459
I break my back for you, sir.

496
00:29:11.459 --> 00:29:13.127
So does my wife.

497
00:29:13.127 --> 00:29:17.131
We even came despite our sister's pregnancy.

498
00:29:17.131 --> 00:29:20.009
This isn't unreasonable.

499
00:29:20.009 --> 00:29:21.427
You work hard for me.

500
00:29:21.427 --> 00:29:24.388
I appreciate it.

501
00:29:24.388 --> 00:29:28.851
Unfortunately, the economy has weathered us all, so no raises.

502
00:29:28.851 --> 00:29:30.060
Sorry.

503
00:29:30.060 --> 00:29:31.353
[VACUUM]

504
00:29:31.353 --> 00:29:31.854
Excuse me.

505
00:29:36.775 --> 00:29:37.276
Jahira!

506
00:29:40.696 --> 00:29:41.197
Jahira!

507
00:29:47.119 --> 00:29:49.580
Jahira!

508
00:29:49.580 --> 00:29:52.541
[VACUUM]

509
00:29:52.541 --> 00:29:53.542
Jahira!

510
00:29:53.542 --> 00:29:54.960
[GRUNT] Where's Mrs. Warren?

511
00:29:54.960 --> 00:29:56.378
Senor, [INAUDIBLE]?

512
00:29:56.378 --> 00:29:59.340
She's in the bed, senor.

513
00:29:59.340 --> 00:30:00.591
Listen, don't clean this room.

514
00:30:00.591 --> 00:30:01.217
OK?

515
00:30:01.217 --> 00:30:02.134
Why, Sir?

516
00:30:02.134 --> 00:30:03.093
I'm almost done.

517
00:30:03.093 --> 00:30:04.678
Well, the lights are broken, so I don't

518
00:30:04.678 --> 00:30:06.388
want you to get electrocuted.

519
00:30:06.388 --> 00:30:08.140
Oh, come on, senor.

520
00:30:08.140 --> 00:30:10.935
I wanted the day off to go see my sister have my nephew,

521
00:30:10.935 --> 00:30:13.145
and you wouldn't give me the day off unless I worked,

522
00:30:13.145 --> 00:30:14.647
because if not, you wouldn't pay me.

523
00:30:14.647 --> 00:30:15.147
Come on.

524
00:30:15.147 --> 00:30:16.106
At least let me finish.

525
00:30:16.106 --> 00:30:17.858
If you don't stop, you're finished.

526
00:30:17.858 --> 00:30:19.818
Wait, don't do that.

527
00:30:19.818 --> 00:30:20.444
Don't do that.

528
00:30:24.698 --> 00:30:28.702
This is what has you all stressed out, senor?

529
00:30:28.702 --> 00:30:32.164
[LAUGHS] [CLEARS THROAT]

530
00:30:32.164 --> 00:30:33.249
Everything all right?

531
00:30:33.249 --> 00:30:34.959
[SPEAKING SPANISH]

532
00:30:37.920 --> 00:30:39.755
Everything's fine, big guy.

533
00:30:47.054 --> 00:30:49.640
You got me.

534
00:30:49.640 --> 00:30:52.434
Mrs. Is really jealous, so I just didn't want her to know.

535
00:30:55.104 --> 00:31:02.152
Look, I have two brothers, two sons, and a husband.

536
00:31:02.152 --> 00:31:03.654
Trust me.

537
00:31:03.654 --> 00:31:05.281
I understand.

538
00:31:05.281 --> 00:31:06.198
[INAUDIBLE]

539
00:31:15.082 --> 00:31:18.502
[MUSIC PLAYING]

540
00:31:35.436 --> 00:31:36.895
(WHISPERING) In the closet.

541
00:31:51.702 --> 00:31:55.080
Everything fine, Mr. Warren?

542
00:31:55.080 --> 00:31:55.581
Sure.

543
00:32:19.188 --> 00:32:23.651
[PHONE RINGING]

544
00:32:23.651 --> 00:32:26.654
Hello.

545
00:32:26.654 --> 00:32:27.154
Yeah.

546
00:32:27.154 --> 00:32:28.155
I'll be right up.

547
00:32:47.591 --> 00:32:48.592
Jahira.

548
00:32:48.592 --> 00:32:49.218
Hey, honey.

549
00:32:49.218 --> 00:32:50.636
You can put it right there.

550
00:32:50.636 --> 00:32:51.887
OK.

551
00:32:51.887 --> 00:32:52.471
Gracias, amor.

552
00:32:55.265 --> 00:32:59.186
[SIGH]

553
00:32:59.186 --> 00:33:02.648
[SPEAKING SPANISH]

554
00:33:26.797 --> 00:33:30.259
[VACUUM]

555
00:34:12.593 --> 00:34:14.595
[GRUNT]

556
00:34:14.595 --> 00:34:18.098
[SPEAKING SPANISH]

557
00:34:36.575 --> 00:34:37.075
